description: Go service discipline for wrapped errors, context on I/O, and module layout.
globs: ["**/*.go", "**/go.mod"]
---

# Go service discipline

Wrap returned errors with fmt.Errorf and `%w` so callers can unwrap.
Do not return bare strings in place of errors.

Pass context.Context through I/O, RPC, and database calls. Do not ignore
err with a blank identifier unless the surrounding package already documents
that case.

Keep module paths and versions consistent with go.mod. Do not add a new
major module path for a local fix.

Match existing layout (cmd, internal, or flat). Do not introduce a
second HTTP router when one already exists.
